\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I am so glad that our father in heaven
\par Tells of His love in the Book He has given:
\par Wonderful things in the Bible I see;
\par This is the dearest, that Jesus loves me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I am so glad that Jesus loves me,
\par Jesus loves even me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though I forget Him, and wander away,
\par Still He doth  love me wherever I stray;
\par Back to His dear loving arms do I flee,
\par When I remember that Jesus loves me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I am so glad that Jesus loves me,
\par Jesus loves even me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O if there's only one song I can sing;
\par When in His beauty I see the great King,
\par This shall my song in eternity be,
\par O what a wonder that Jesus loves me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I am so glad that Jesus loves me,
\par Jesus loves even me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If one should ask me: How can I tell?
\par Glory to Jesus, I know very well;
\par God's Holy Spirit with mine doth agree,
\par Constantly witnessing: Jesus loves me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I am so glad that Jesus loves me,
\par Jesus loves even me.
\par \f1 
